The lift, verbatim (new static helper placed BEFORE PlaceItem so MWCC's defined-before-inline rule applies):
`static s32 FindInfoIndex(s32 type, s32 level, char* name)
{
    iteminfo* def;
    s32 i;

    def = gWorldInfo.iteminfo;

    for (i = 0; i < gWorldInfo.niteminfos; i++, def++) {
        iteminfodata* body = &def->item;
        if (strcmp(name, body->desc) != 0) {
            continue;
        }
        if (type != def->type) {
            continue;
        }
        if (level <= 0 || level == body->subtype) {
            return i;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}`
and PlaceItem reduced to `i = FindInfoIndex(type, level, name);` replacing the inline loop plus its `i = -1; found:` scaffolding.
NAME PROVENANCE: `FindInfoIndex` is the Xbox PDB's own name for this operation in the same module -- research/xbox_symbols/functions_by_module.txt line 4253, `[0001:000407C0] 79 G FindInfoIndex` in ITEMS.OBJ. It is `static` here because the GC target's items.c roster (python tools/gdl/fnasm.py game/world/items) carries no such symbol, i.e. the GC build inlined and dead-stripped it.
